The fixed heap address of ghc-bootstrap's rts/patches/0003-mblock-map-window.patch
for aarch64 as well.  A non-PIE aarch64 Linux process has the x86-64 layout:
the executable at 0x400000, the C heap after it and the mmap area at the top of
the address space, so 0x500000000 lies between them.  Without it the heap
comes from an unhinted mmap, outside the window the mblock map covers, and
getMBlocks fails at once.

--- a/ghc/rts/MBlock.h
+++ b/ghc/rts/MBlock.h
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 #error I have no idea where to begin the heap on a non-64-bit osf3 machine.
 #endif
 
-#elif defined(x86_64_TARGET_ARCH) && SIZEOF_VOID_P == 8
+#elif (defined(x86_64_TARGET_ARCH) || defined(aarch64_TARGET_ARCH)) && SIZEOF_VOID_P == 8
 /* Ask for the heap from a fixed address, as 6.4 does on x86-64: above the
  * executable and the C heap (a non-PIE binary sits at 0x400000 and brk
  * grows from its end) and below the mmap area (0x7f...).  With HEAP_BASE 0
